184
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:17,407
Your assignment has four questions. One: sewing at 3500 r/min,

185
00:16:17,427 --> 00:16:25,638
work out stage by stage the stop-and-trim time for trimming speeds of 250 and

186
00:16:25,658 --> 00:16:26,707
400 r/min.

187
00:16:26,727 --> 00:16:33,121
With 2500 trims a day, how many minutes a day separate them?

188
00:16:33,521 --> 00:16:39,288
Two: trimming at 450 r/min with a 6 to 9 millisecond delay.

189
00:16:39,308 --> 00:16:44,780
Find the allowed range of command angles and choose one.

190
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:51,842
After a while a low voltage stretches the delay to 5 to 13 milliseconds.

191
00:16:51,862 --> 00:16:58,021
Does your angle still work? If not, change it, and explain why.

192
00:16:58,421 --> 00:17:03,581
Three: with an idle angle of 211.6 degrees and a 10-degree margin,

193
00:17:03,601 --> 00:17:08,918
find the backtack speed limits for a reverse-feed solenoid with a 16

194
00:17:08,938 --> 00:17:13,941
millisecond delay and a feed stepper with a 5 millisecond delay,

195
00:17:13,961 --> 00:17:19,436
then say why an electronic-feed machine may still default to only 1800

196
00:17:19,456 --> 00:17:22,653
stitches a minute for the start backtack.

197
00:17:22,673 --> 00:17:27,912
Four is a discussion. At a cross seam the machine lowers the speed,

198
00:17:27,932 --> 00:17:32,386
adds foot pressure and changes the needle-thread tension.

199
00:17:32,406 --> 00:17:38,272
Say which fault each one prevents, which way it goes, and its side effects.

200
00:17:38,672 --> 00:17:44,772
Submit the calculation report and the lab screenshots on the WenQuest platform.

201
00:17:46,292 --> 00:17:50,793
There's also a ten-question quiz. For example,

202
00:17:50,813 --> 00:17:57,378
trimming at 500 r/min with the command at 285 degrees and a 6 to 10

203
00:17:57,398 --> 00:17:59,147
millisecond delay:

204
00:17:59,167 --> 00:18:03,963
at what angle does the knife enter at the latest?

205
00:18:04,363 --> 00:18:04,611
Or,

206
00:18:04,631 --> 00:18:11,842
the delay varies between 7 and 12 milliseconds and the window is 30 degrees wide.

207
00:18:11,862 --> 00:18:17,555
Considering only the window, what is the highest trimming speed?

208
00:18:17,955 --> 00:18:22,855
You get three attempts, and the explanations appear as soon as you submit.

209
00:18:24,375 --> 00:18:26,675
Three things to remember.

210
00:18:27,075 --> 00:18:31,376
One: a state machine sequences the working cycle,

211
00:18:31,396 --> 00:18:37,020
and in stop-and-trim the trimming stitch takes most of the time.

212
00:18:37,420 --> 00:18:44,904
Two: every action lines up with the mechanical timing chart:

213
00:18:44,924 --> 00:18:50,156
reversal inside the feed dog's idle angle,

214
00:18:50,176 --> 00:18:56,159
knife entry inside the 300-to-330-degree window.

215
00:18:56,559 --> 00:19:01,015
Three: entry angle equals command angle plus 6 n t;

216
00:19:01,035 --> 00:19:03,999
the mean delay can be compensated,

217
00:19:04,019 --> 00:19:10,844
but its spread can only be absorbed by slowing down, so keep the delay steady.

